face-image: img/hitler_prozess.jpg

= The Hitler-Ludendorff Trial

[? if hitler_prozess_court == "Munich": Ludenforff was immediadetly freed from custody - there are rumors that his honest testimony was replaced with one that makes him appear innocent. Meanwhile Hitler claimed full responsibility for the coup attempt turning the court room into a stage for his only moderately interesting, quite uncreative, speeches attacking both the <style="color: [+ spd_colour +];">**SPD**</span> and *unpatriotic* <span style="color: [+ bvp_colour +];">Triumvirate</span>. ?]

[? if hitler_prozess_court == "Munich": The coup leaders return for their ruling, Ludendorff is even wearing his wartime uniform. Let's hope for a somewhat sensible sentence... ?]

[? if hitler_prozess_court == "Leipzig": Somehow we have actually gotten the coup leaders to Leipzig, the heart of the Republican Judiciary. (This is one of those points where I would make up some kind of text but I'm just going with the coding holding this open for another day - use your imagination, you little waffel) ?]



- @hit_leipzig_ruling: The judge rules...
- @hit_munich_ruling: The judge rules...

@hit_munich_ruling
view-if: hitler_prozess_court == "Munich"
on-arrival: old_middle_nsdap += 3; rural_nsdap += 2

Ludendorff is freed of all charges - he immediately protests feeling insulted by the ignorance towards his perceived honour and hard work. Hitler who should be deported to Austria according to law is only given the basic sentence of five years in prison with a possibility of being freed earlier. Most other leaders have gotten similar rulings.

- @tffffffffff: This is stupid.

@tffffffffff

@hit_leipzig_ruling
view-if: hitler_prozess_court == "Leipzig"
on-arrival: bvp_relation -= 4; dvp_relation -= 3; dnvp_relation -= 2; hitler_prozess_chances += judiciary_reform; hitler_deported = 1

Hitler will be deported to Austria. As a foreign citizen charged for high treason he has no right to remain in the Reich.

- @ludendorff_does_nothing: And the others?
- @milder_sentence: And the others?
- @harsher_sentence: And the others?

@ludendorff_does_nothing
view-if: hitler_prozess_chances <= 0
on-arrival: old_middle_nsdap += 2; old_middle_dvfp += 2

While most <span style="color: [+ nsdap_colour +];">**NSDAP**</span>-members are given a moderate prison sentence, Ludendorff goes free. It appears some of the judges might still hold respect for the veteran. Ludendorff protests loudly claiming full responsibility for the coup but nobody seems to listen... 

@milder_sentence
view-if: hitler_prozess_chances > 0 and hitler_prozess_chances < 6
on-arrival: ludendorff_prison_timer = 96

The conspirators are given a prison sentence of eight years each and some moderate fines. While there is an outcry among sympathizers, Ludendorff especially seems to very proud of his jail time.

@harsher_sentence
view-if: hitler_prozess_chances >= 6
on-arrival: ludendorff_prison_timer = 144

The conspirators are given a prison sentence of twelve years each and some moderate fines. The outcry among sympathizers is immense while the condemmend seem to accept their newfound political irrelevance as punishment for their terribly planned coup...




